  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council (whole council, two wards), polled Monday 15 January 1923. The five Unionist candidates for East Ward were returned unopposed; the seven West Ward seats were contested by seven Labour and two Unionist candidates, and all seven Labour men were returned. All seven Labour (anti-Partitionist) candidates were returned. The earlier transcription (from the faint News-Letter image) had Savage 256, Williams 250, E. Caulfield 253, T. H. Caulfield 243, Mather 163, Wilson 160; the Newry Telegraph figures are clear and are used. The two Caulfields tied on 258 for the last two seats, both elected."
